  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DRC-Goma Acute Crisis Joint Response DRA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated Health/WASH emergency response in Karisimbi Health Zone and based on own needs assessments with focus on Bujovu and Majengo health areas. HEALTH: primary healthcare in 2 HFs through free consultations to beneficiaries through outpatient consultations (OC), childhood disease control, referrals, emergency reproductive health (prevention &amp; management of sexual violence &lt;72 hours, improve maternal and newborn health). Epidemic prevention with vaccination for children &lt;5 and pregnant women (PLW).IPC: In the two HFs, Infection Prevention and Control measures are enhanced through provision of Personal Protective Equipment, disinfectants and waste management supplies. Community awareness campaigns enhance epidemic outbreak prevention.WASH: safe water and hygiene in homes and HFs through water trucking, water quality monitoring, and water chlorination to limit spread of waterborne diseases. Chlorination points are based on existing water points. Promotion of hygiene, incl. menstrual hygiene and distribution of jerricans for transport, storage and recipient for waste management.</narrative>
  </description>
